## 1. The decisions that matter most

1. **One clock.** A fixed 60-tick-per-second simulation; 1x and 2x are "how many ticks per frame"; pause is zero ticks. Combat has no randomness. Attacks resolve in the tick they fire (there are no simulated projectiles).
2. **One route, 16 pads, opened in stages.** The route is {{F:routeLength}} tiles long. Six good pads are open at the start and two more open with each new class (after waves 5, 10, 15, 20 and 25). The first screen stays simple for a five-year-old and every newly unlocked class has a free pad waiting. Fallback: open all 16 from wave 1, which is one data value per pad; in the simulator the naive player then gets less far (16.3).
3. **Unlock order kept as proposed**: Nova at the start, then Pip, Juno, Orion, Mira, Sol after waves 5, 10, 15, 20 and 25. The first four unlocks all add firepower, so a child who always buys "the new one" has attackers before the two non-attacking classes arrive.
4. **Small deployment caps keep the team mixed**: Pip 3, Juno 4, Orion 3, Mira 2, Sol 2; Nova uncapped.
5. **Credits come from two places only**: defeated aliens and successful normal learning activities (CONFIRMED prompt.md:447). No wave-clear bonus. A run starts with {{F:startCredits}}. The campaign offers {{F:bountyTotal}} credits of bounty and {{F:learnTotal}} of learning rewards; the reference 16-astronaut level-3 board costs {{F:fieldCost}}.
6. **Selling returns 70% of everything paid for that astronaut, rounded down to a multiple of 5.** Sell-then-rebuy always loses credits (proof in 5.7).
7. **The colony has {{F:maxHealth}} health and up to {{F:shieldCap}} shield points.** Small aliens cost 1 health; the five bosses cost {{F:bossLeakList}}. A boss that gets through is a heavy blow, not an automatic defeat, except the last one against an unshielded colony.
8. **Six alien traits, each a single exact rule**: armour (flat reduction), bubble layers (absorb a number of hits), flying (halves Juno's blast), healer (shared 3-second pulse), splitter, carrier. Each rewards a different class without requiring it.
9. **Five bosses built only from those traits.** No new routes, projectiles or pad effects.
10. **Meteor powers follow a fixed rotation** (Frost Pulse, Comet Burst, Colony Shield, ...): one charge per successful meteor challenge, kept until used, at most two of each.
11. **Endless continuation is a pure function of the wave number**, built from waves 41-49 and the five bosses, with caps reached at waves {{F:endlessCaps.speed}} (speed), {{F:endlessCaps.count}} (counts), {{F:endlessCaps.boss}} (boss health) and {{F:endlessCaps.hp}} (health).
12. **Simulator verdict against the design targets** (SIM, section 16). Competent player, 0% learning, no powers: clears wave {{F:c0.cleared}} with {{F:c0.health}} health; smallest margin {{F:marginMin}}. Competent, 60%: clears with {{F:c60.health}} health. Naive child, 60%: clears between {{F:naive60.min}} and {{F:naive60.max}} waves over {{F:naive60.n}} seeds, median {{F:naive60.median}}, and {{F:naive60.ge30}} of {{F:naive60.n}} reach wave 30. Every boss is beaten without powers and with any one class removed. The soft spots are listed plainly in 16.6.

