## 4. The colony

| Rule | Value |
|---|---|
| Health | {{F:maxHealth}} (an integer). 0 or less is defeat, which is terminal for the run (CONFIRMED prompt.md:675). |
| Shield points | Separate from health, capped at {{F:shieldCap}}. Leak damage comes off shield points first, then health. |
| Sources of shield | Mira's pulses (5.5) and the Colony Shield power (section 10). The power may lift the shield to an absolute cap of {{F:shieldAbs}} for the rest of that wave; anything above {{F:shieldCap}} is removed when the wave ends. |
| Between waves | Health and shield carry over unchanged (both are in the snapshot). Nothing regenerates while preparing. |
| Repair | +{{F:bossRepair}} health when a boss wave is completed, whether or not the boss was defeated; +1 health per completed wave while a level-3 Mira is deployed (at most 1 per wave in total). Never above {{F:maxHealth}}. |
| Leak damage | Per alien type (section 6): 1 for small aliens, 2 for sturdy ones, 4 for an Alien Craft, {{F:bossLeakList}} for the five bosses. |

No alien damages, disables or blocks an astronaut or a pad: nothing in this design lets anything except a player command change an astronaut (CONFIRMED prompt.md:297, AC-07).

Why 20 and these leak values: a child can let twenty Moon Blobs through over a run before losing, which is a great deal of forgiveness early on; and a boss leak of 8 to 14 leaves a healthy colony standing, so failing to stop a boss is a setback to recover from, not the end of a long run. The small repair after each boss makes clearing a boss feel good and gives a struggling player something back.

